                <note rend="inline" type="source">894.001H61/79: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Neville</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-08-13T18:00:00+09:00">August 13, 1935—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 13—5:52 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>167. The recent alleged disrespect of the Japanese Emperor at Seattle was
                    featured in the Japanese newspapers of August 10 and 12 but has not been
                    mentioned since the publication of a statement to the effect that Hornbeck
                    expressed to the Japanese Counselor a desire for local settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Neville</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
